- Hemoptysis supports bronchiectasis or NTM;  
- Dyspnea/wheeze suggests asthma-COPD overlap or ABPA;  
- Chronic sinusitis points to CF or allergic fungal disease;  
- Weight loss/night sweats raise concern for infection (e.g., TB, NTM) or malignancy;  
- Clubbing would further support chronic suppurative lung disease.  
I’ll ask a targeted, atomic question covering the most discriminating systemic and respiratory-associated symptoms.

[QUERY] Have you noticed any blood in your sputum, shortness of breath with usual activities, wheezing, frequent sinus infections or nasal congestion, unexplained weight loss, drenching night sweats, or swelling or rounding of your fingertips?

